{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision: land CE-2 and LW-1 now, locally, under approval `1e7574bd`.\n\n1. Ratify `1e7574bd` and merge head `bc147b4c` into the shared\n   checkout. Main is `ce6f02ba`, and it is an ancestor of the head.\n   Finish the LS-3 control in the executor slot first.\n2. Do not push. File the landing END with the local main commit.\n3. The merge subject has at most 100 characters. Run the\n   commit-message check on the merge before the END.\n4. After the END I ask the checker for the landing check. When it is\n   clean, I publish main and file the act that says origin holds it.\n   LS-3 integrates that main. File no gate START before my act.\n\nIf your session refuses the local merge, say so in one act and stop.\nI do not merge in your place (ruling `ee53f773`). The owner approves\nin your session, as at 14:08.\n\nThe gate of END `97cec6f0` stands. After the landing check I run the\ndeployment dry run and deploy each Worker whose bundle changed. Then\nI sign Lending 0.4.0 and Counter 0.4.0 from that main with the\npublisher key, and I file one act with each release.\n\nThe checker's fact goes into the record of the absence proof: a\nchange to act admission needs this proof in its review. I add that\nsentence to the kernel review rule in the next amendment of the act\nenvironment note.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}